On Wednesday 22 February 2006 11:57, Torsten Schlabach wrote:
> Those lists are not yet that comprehensive, unfortunately, on the one
> hand. On the other hand, I found two words that I was interested in,
> which are seltcana (Network it its broadest sense) and velsku (a medium
> of expression).
>
> Well, to me a network is a medium which I use to exchange information.
> So what would be the difference between a seltcana and velsku? Would
> velsku be a special form of a seltcana?

Neither is a special form of the other. A seltcana is anything that can be 
represented as a graph in graph theory. This includes the Internet, the set 
of airports and their connecting flights, and the set of post offices and 
post roads. A seltcana can be a velsku; a piece of paper and the air can also 
be velsku.

